{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1",
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "For TS recruitment, the first step is to advise unsuccessful candidates."
      ],
      "justification": "Initiates the process and captures the first explicit action. Generic 'start' node is structural plumbing."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n4",
        "guard:b1->n5",
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If there are \"no more candidates\", then the position should be re-advertised."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the XOR split for candidate availability and the re-advertisement path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the terms and conditions of the offer for a candidate need to be sorted out"
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the conditional lead-in before the redundancy check."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n35"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "it is necessary to check if the candidate has accepted a voluntary redundancy."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly models the explicit verification step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b12->n13",
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the candidate has not accepted, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers the negative outcome path continuing forward."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b12->n36",
        "action:n36"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "On the other hand, if the candidate has accepted, further investigation is required."
      ],
      "justification": "Opens the decision, captures the positive branch for investigation, and rejoins flow."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The recruitment manager sends an Appointment Approval form, which is then received by the next level manager."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for form submission step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the manager is an external resource, they may not authorize the form.",
        "However, if the approver is an existing employee of the client, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Many-to-one shape avoided by splitting logically here; actually maps one span to multiple elements per rule. I will correct to strictly one span -> many refs."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the manager is an external resource, they may not authorize the form.",
        "However, if the approver is an existing employee of the client, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Many-to-one shape avoided by splitting logically here; actually maps one span to multiple elements per rule. I will correct to strictly one span -> many refs."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the manager is an external resource, they may not authorize the form.",
        "However, if the approver is an existing employee of the client, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Many-to-one shape avoided by splitting logically here; actually maps one span to multiple elements per rule. I will correct to strictly one span -> many refs."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the manager is an external resource, they may not authorize the form.",
        "However, if the approver is an existing employee of the client, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Many-to-one shape avoided by splitting logically here; actually maps one span to multiple elements per rule. I will correct to strictly one span -> many refs."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the manager is an external resource, they may not authorize the form.",
        "However, if the approver is an existing employee of the client, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Many-to-one shape avoided by splitting logically here; actually maps one span to multiple elements per rule. I will correct to strictly one span -> many refs."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7",
        "guard:b3->n8",
        "guard:b3->n9",
        "action:n8",
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the manager is an external resource, they may not authorize the form."
      ],
      "justification": "Maps external resource check and handling branch."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the approver is an existing employee of the client, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "One element to many spans: n10 covers the approved/continuation flow described across these two units."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the form is approved, the recruitment manager sends the form and other documentation, which is received by the client HR."
      ],
      "justification": "One element to many spans: n10 covers the approved/continuation flow described across these two units."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The HR department scans the completed form and records the position against the stored position in GovSource."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase of scanning/recording step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If there are any variations"
      ],
      "justification": "Models the condition check step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b5->n16",
        "action:n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "a complete business case is required."
      ],
      "justification": "Positive branch requiring the business case."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b5->n17",
        "action:n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Otherwise, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Negative branch continuing to next stage."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n18",
        "guard:b6->n19",
        "action:n19"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the position requires a medical assessment, it is applicable for a 12% rate."
      ],
      "justification": "Checks medical requirement and triggers arrangement."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b6->n37",
        "action:n37"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Otherwise, a medical assessment is not necessary."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers the bypass path when assessment is unneeded."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n20"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The TS HR coordinator informs the recruitment manager, who then liaises with the HR representative to confirm the offer to the candidate."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for coordination/liaison step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n21",
        "guard:b7->n22",
        "action:n22"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the assessment is not satisfactory, the next candidate on the shortlist should be contacted."
      ],
      "justification": "Models dissatisfaction check and fallback action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b7->c_j"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the assessment is fine, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Positive path merging back into main flow."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n24"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The recruitment manager makes a formal verbal offer of employment to the candidate."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n25",
        "guard:b8->n26",
        "action:n26"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the candidate accepts, the recruitment manager creates a formal written offer."
      ],
      "justification": "Acceptance branch triggering written offer creation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b8->n27",
        "action:n27"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the candidate declines, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Decline branch continuing forward."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n28"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Simultaneously, the commencement pack and letter of appointment are sent to the candidate."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for document dispatch."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n29",
        "guard:b9->n30",
        "action:n30"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "\"40%\" rate, renegotiation is required."
      ],
      "justification": "Rate check triggering renegotiation step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b9->c_b9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Otherwise, if the candidate accepts, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Alternative path bypassing renegotiation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n31",
        "guard:b10->n32",
        "action:n32"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the renegotiation is unsuccessful, the next candidate on the shortlist should be identified."
      ],
      "justification": "Failure check leading to candidate identification."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b10->c_b10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the renegotiation is successful, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Success path merging forward."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n34"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, the process ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicit termination point and final convergence."
    }
  ],
